{
 "_derivation": {
  "author": "independent second agent (CD-2 continuous --skip-generate golden), derived by reading lane/v17-run-cd2 at 3b090ab (src unchanged) plus the uncommitted harness diff (SCENARIOS['continuous_c360_skip_generate']) and starting from the confirmed tests/fixtures/run_char/continuous_c360.json; the harness, test_run_characterisation.py, run(), _run_sustained and the CLI were not run.",
  "tree": "lane/v17-run-cd2 at 3b090ab, src unchanged; harness diff uncommitted",
  "scenario": "continuous_c360 with --skip-generate added: same config, logs, clock start and FakeTrino answers (run_harness.py SCENARIOS['continuous_c360_skip_generate']).",
  "delta_calls": "Four changes, net 236 calls (238 - 3 + 1). (1) run() reads the datagen Job before the prerequisites: _use_sustained and skip_generate, so _datagen_job_state(namespace) (cli/_run.py:1840-1844, cli/_sustained.py:417-442) -> BatchV1Api read_namespaced_job lakebench-datagen runchar, inserted at index 2 after get_cluster_capacity; FakeBatchV1Api answers Complete (run_harness.py:501-509), state 'finished', so datagen_runs False. (2) prerequisites args {sustained True, datagen_runs False} (cli/_run.py:1845). (3) _c360_existing_state(clear_raw=not skip_generate = False) (cli/_sustained.py:2846, 352-394) lists 5 prefixes, not the raw landing zone customer/interactions/. (4) _reset_continuous_state(clear_raw=False) (cli/_sustained.py:2863, 305-349) deletes the three checkpoints only, not the raw prefix. (5) The skip_generate branch (cli/_sustained.py:2864-2866) prints instead of DatagenDeployer(engine).deploy(): the Datagen deploy call is gone (FakeDatagenDeployer.__init__ records nothing, so only the deploy entry goes). DeploymentEngine(cfg) is still built before the reset (cli/_sustained.py:2833), so its get_k8s_client, get_cluster_capacity and ApisApi calls stay.",
  "unchanged_calls": "The ownership checks, _stop_leftover_streams, the c360 reset preflight (bronze-verify, 5400 s), and _datagen_released(deployed_here=False) (cli/_sustained.py:2972-2974, 450-483): the Job reads Complete, 'finished' releases whatever deployed_here is, one BatchV1Api read as before, no sleep. collect_from_k8s still runs at window end (cli/_sustained.py:3382-3390, not conditional on skip_generate), so _datagen_output_rows, the settle budget and every later call are the record's.",
  "journal_events": "unchanged: GENERATE_START is journalled after the if/else (cli/_sustained.py:2880-2889), so generate.start stays even though datagen is not deployed; streaming.start's datagen_cores_reserved is False as before (not traced).",
  "values_and_sections": "unchanged. Nothing between the datagen read and the window advances FakeClock (the extra read is instant), so the loop schedule, rounds, maintenance, settle (870 s), window and every score are as continuous_c360. skip_generate is read nowhere else in _run_sustained (grep: lines 2846, 2863, 2864, 2973 only), and the fleet rows that size the settle come from collect_from_k8s, not from the deploy. exit_code, unscripted, runs_saved, exported_run_id, submits, journal_events, metrics_keys, jobs, maintenance_outcomes, values, c360_correctness, success, verdict, verdict_reasons, continuous, streaming, benchmark_rounds and continuous_scores are byte-for-byte continuous_c360's.",
  "differs_from_record": "As continuous_c360's differs_from_record (settle 870.0 s vs 874.1, total_s3_objects 300 vs 12320, constant gold event age, throughput over exactly 1800.0 s, round and skip times, window start .500). In addition the record deployed datagen itself (no --skip-generate) and cleared the raw prefix; this scenario does neither and replays the record's fleet as if a finished datagen Job wrote it.",
  "unsure": "Nothing material. The only judgement is that a 'finished' datagen Job makes run() pass datagen_runs=False to the prerequisites, which the code states directly (cli/_run.py:1844).",
  "calls_count": "236 calls (continuous_c360: 238)",
  "rerecord_sd8": "SD-8 (integrate 2f28d4e, merged before this golden) moved one call and nothing else: _run_sustained now only builds the scripts maps (build_script_configmaps, pure, reads the packaged scripts, cli/_sustained.py:2828) where it used to deploy them, and deploys them (JobManager.deploy_scripts_configmap, cli/_sustained.py:2875) after _stop_leftover_streams and _reset_continuous_state (:2868-2869), so a changed map is not replaced while a leftover stream still mounts it. In calls the deploy_scripts_configmap entry moves from after Benchmark init to after the last reset delete_prefix, before the reset preflight's bronze-verify submit (no Datagen deploy under --skip-generate). Call count unchanged (236); every other section is unchanged. Moved by hand from the SD-8 diff, then checked against the harness on b587651. Line citations in the other _derivation keys are against the tree named in 'tree' (pre-SD-8): on b587651 cli/_sustained.py lines from about 2823 to 2867 sit 6 lower and lines after 2867 sit 21 lower (DatagenDeployer.deploy is now 2891-2892, the reset preflight about 2979-2986), and cli/_run.py lines after 1999 sit 8 lower. The early build_script_configmaps call is real code in the harness, not a seam, so it is not in calls; removing it would not move this golden.",
  "rerecord_cd16": "CD-16 with LB-233 (lane/v17-run-cd16): journal_events[2] generate.start removed, by hand from the code. With --skip-generate no datagen is deployed, and the GENERATE_START 'Datagen started for continuous pipeline' record now sits inside the branch that deploys it (cli/_sustained.py, after RunInterrupt.datagen_created). calls do not move: the skip branch makes no datagen deploy and so no uid read. The counts in calls_count and delta_calls were written against continuous_c360 at 238 calls; since CD-16 that golden has 239 (its extra call is the datagen uid read after Datagen deploy, which --skip-generate does not make), so the delta from it is now net 236 = 239 - 3 (as before) + 1 - 1 (no uid read); this golden still has 236.",
  "rerecord_cd17": "CD-17 (lane/v17-run-cd16, stacked on CD-16): 49 CoreV1Api read_namespace runchar calls added, by hand from the loop_schedule above, not from the harness. NamespaceWatch.start() reads the namespace once after stream_identities (the window start), and check() reads it after every loop sleep before the health line, and at the top of every benchmark round, maintenance round and compaction round that runs (cli/_sustained.py). From the schedule: start + 10 health probes (30..300) + round-1 probe before round 1; 6 health probes (466.5..600) + maintenance-1 probe before maintenance 1; 5 (630..736.5) + round-2 probe before round 2; 10 (898.1..1168.1) + round-3 probe before round 3; the maintenance-2 probe and the compaction probe of the 1326.1 iteration before their calls; 11 health probes (1519.1..1626.1, 1656.1..1776.1, 1800.0) before the window-end get_job_status. The round due at 1626.1 is skipped (late) and gets no round probe. Nothing else moves."
 },
